<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14971" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρή</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], ἡ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bane, ruin,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρὴν ἑτάροισιν ἀμύνειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					12.334
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρῆς ἀλκτῆρα γενέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					18.100
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρὴν καὶ λοιγὸν ἀμῦναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					24.489
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				2.59
			</span></i>; so in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				84
			</span></i> (lyr.), where the gloss of the Sch., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βλάβης,</span> confirms the reading <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρῆς</span> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρης.</span>
			(Cf. pf.
			part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ̄ρημένος</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βεβλαμμένος</span>
			, and pr. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄρης</span> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				Corn.
				<u>ND</u>
				20
			</span></i>), perh. also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρος, ἀρειά,
				ἐπήρεια</span>; perh. an old <i>ē</i>
		stem.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
